<!-- FAQ -->
<section class="section bg-surface">
  <div class="container-narrow mx-auto px-4">
    <h2 class="text-center mb-8">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <div class="space-y-3 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <details class="card group cursor-pointer"><summary class="font-semibold text-primary hover:text-accent">What is the DAC in CJC-1295?</summary><p class="mt-3 text-gray-600 text-sm">DAC stands for Drug Affinity Complex — a maleimidopropionyl linker that covalently binds to Cys³⁴ of serum albumin. This conjugation extends half-life from minutes to ~8 days by preventing renal clearance and enzymatic degradation.</p></details>
      <details class="card group cursor-pointer"><summary class="font-semibold text-primary hover:text-accent">Difference between CJC-1295 with DAC and without DAC?</summary><p class="mt-3 text-gray-600 text-sm">With DAC: ~8 day half-life → sustained GHRH activation → chronic GH/IGF-1. Without DAC: ~30 min half-life → discrete GH pulse → mimics endogenous pulsatile secretion. Choice depends on research objective.</p></details>
      <details class="card group cursor-pointer"><summary class="font-semibold text-primary hover:text-accent">Why pair CJC-1295 with Ipamorelin?</summary><p class="mt-3 text-gray-600 text-sm">CJC-1295 amplifies the GHRH signal (the 'on' switch). Ipamorelin suppresses somatostatin tone (the 'off' switch). Together they produce a larger net GH pulse than either alone — well-characterized synergism.</p></details>
      <details class="card group cursor-pointer"><summary class="font-semibold text-primary hover:text-accent">How should CJC-1295 (DAC) be stored?</summary><p class="mt-3 text-gray-600 text-sm">Lyophilized: 2–8°C, desiccated, 24-month stability. After reconstitution, store at 2–8°C. The DAC-albumin conjugate forms spontaneously — this is expected and part of the molecule's designed mechanism.</p></details>
      <details class="card group cursor-pointer"><summary class="font-semibold text-primary hover:text-accent">What configurations are available?</summary><p class="mt-3 text-gray-600 text-sm">Standard: 2mg × 10 vials. Bulk: 5mg × 10 vials. Custom mg/vial for OEM/private-label. CJC-1295 (no DAC) also available as a separate SKU for pulsatile GH protocols.</p></details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Related Products -->
<section class="section bg-white">
  <div class="container-wide mx-auto px-4">
    <h2 class="text-center mb-6">Related Products</h2>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-4 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <a href="/products/muscle-growth/" class="card p-4 text-center hover:border-accent/30 transition-colors"><span class="font-semibold text-primary block">Ipamorelin</span><span class="text-gray-500 text-xs">Selective GHS-R agonist</span></a>
      <a href="/products/muscle-growth/" class="card p-4 text-center hover:border-accent/30 transition-colors"><span class="font-semibold text-primary block">GHRP-2</span><span class="text-gray-500 text-xs">Potent GHS-R agonist</span></a>
      <a href="/products/hgh/" class="card p-4 text-center hover:border-accent/30 transition-colors"><span class="font-semibold text-primary block">HGH</span><span class="text-gray-500 text-xs">Direct GH receptor agonist</span></a>
      <a href="/products/muscle-growth/" class="card p-4 text-center hover:border-accent/30 transition-colors"><span class="font-semibold text-primary block">Muscle Category</span><span class="text-gray-500 text-xs">All GH peptides</span></a>
